lilith-rice: bar logo, window title and REC modules; natural scrolling per device type

Bar (src/bar.h, src/lilith.c):
  BarModLogo   static text (barlogo, config/config_bar.h)
  BarModTitle  title of the focused window, or bartitlefallback ("desktop"); kept current
               from printstatus() (focus, title and tag changes)
  BarModRec    red "REC" badge, shown while the status line on stdin starts with "REC|"
               (lilith-status prints that prefix while lilith-record is recording)
Input (src/lilith.c):
  natural scrolling is chosen per device: touchpads use natural_scrolling_touchpad, mice use
  natural_scrolling_mouse (upstream applies one value to every pointer).

Applied by `lilith-rice build` with `patch -p1 -F0`, all or nothing. If it does not apply or
compile, the installer builds stock lilith: the three bar modules stay empty and natural
scrolling follows the stock natural_scrolling value.

